# SQL's uppercase `NULLS FIRST` / `NULLS LAST` after a sort key: DS0105 with a fix to lowercase,
# and the key still parses.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | sort by amount desc NULLS FIRST, orderId asc nulls LAST
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..76
  PIPELINE@0..75
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    SORT_OP@20..75
      IDENT@20..24 "sort"
      WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
      IDENT@25..27 "by"
      WHITESPACE@27..28 " "
      SORT_KEY@28..51
        NAME_REF@28..34
          IDENT@28..34 "amount"
        WHITESPACE@34..35 " "
        IDENT@35..39 "desc"
        WHITESPACE@39..40 " "
        IDENT@40..45 "NULLS"
        WHITESPACE@45..46 " "
        IDENT@46..51 "FIRST"
      COMMA@51..52 ","
      WHITESPACE@52..53 " "
      SORT_KEY@53..75
        NAME_REF@53..60
          IDENT@53..60 "orderId"
        WHITESPACE@60..61 " "
        IDENT@61..64 "asc"
        WHITESPACE@64..65 " "
        IDENT@65..70 "nulls"
        WHITESPACE@70..71 " "
        IDENT@71..75 "LAST"
  WHITESPACE@75..76 "\n"

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `NULLS FIRST` in capitals
  --> query:1:41
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | sort by amount desc NULLS FIRST, orderId asc nulls LAST
  |                                         ^^^^^^^^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: keywords are lowercase: write `nulls first`

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `nulls LAST` in capitals
  --> query:1:66
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | sort by amount desc NULLS FIRST, orderId asc nulls LAST
  |                                                                  ^^^^^^^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: keywords are lowercase: write `nulls last`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | sort by amount desc nulls first, orderId asc nulls last
which parses without errors
